## Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery

The mission is decomposed into a hierarchy of **goals** (high‑level intentions) and **tasks** (atomic, executable actions).  
Each goal is annotated with its **runtime** (execution structure over its children), **goal type** (Achieve / Perform / Query), and **justification**.  
Each task is linked to its parent goal, specifies the **location** where it is executed and the **number of robots** required, together with a short justification.

> **Notation**  
> *Runtime*: `#` = parallel, `;` = sequential, `FALLBACK(exp1,exp2)` = binary fallback.  
> *Leaf goal* → runtime `-`.  
> *Relation* between parent and child → `AND` or `OR`.  

---

### 1. Goal Table

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Target Condition / Enquired Info | Relation | Justification |
|------|------|---------|-----------|----------------------------------|----------|---------------|
| **G1: Complete Resource Delivery Mission** | Deliver the requested resources from storage to the requesting agent at the specified location. | `;` | Achieve | *Resources delivered to requesting agent at specified location.* | — | The mission is finished only after collection **and** delivery are completed, hence a sequential decomposition. |
| **G2: Collect Resources** | Collect the required resources from storage locations. | `;` | Perform | — | AND | All sub‑steps of collection (planning, navigation, request, wait, pickup, low‑battery handling, hand‑over) must be executed. |
| **G3: Deliver Resources** | Deliver the collected resources to the requesting agent at the specified location. | `;` | Perform | — | AND | All sub‑steps of delivery (navigation, hand‑over, low‑battery handling, final delivery) must be executed. |
| **G2.1: Determine Order to Follow** | Estimate waiting time and path to determine order of storage visits. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Needed before any robot can navigate to a storage location. |
| **G2.2: Navigate to Storage Location** | Move the robot to the storage location where resources are located. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Physical movement is mandatory to reach the storage. |
| **G2.3: Request Resource from Storage** | Send a message to storage specifying the resources requested. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | The robot must request the resources before they can be retrieved. |
| **G2.4: Wait for Retrieval** | Wait until the resources are retrieved from storage. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | The robot must wait for confirmation before proceeding. |
| **G2.5: Pick Up Resource** | Pick up the retrieved resources. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Physical pickup is required before delivery. |
| **G2.6: Handle Low Battery During Collection** | If battery low during collection, either recharge or hand over mission. | `FALLBACK(G2.6.1, G2.6.2)` | Perform | — | AND | Two alternatives are explicitly specified in the mission description. |
| **G2.6.1: Return to Recharging Station** | Return to recharging station to recharge battery. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Battery < 10 % → recharge. |
| **G2.6.2: Assign Mission to Another Robot** | Assign the remaining collection task to another robot. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Alternative if recharge is not possible or not timely. |
| **G3.1: Navigate to Delivery Location** | Move the robot to the destination location where resources must be delivered. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Physical movement to the delivery point is mandatory. |
| **G3.2: Deliver Resource** | Deliver the resources to the requesting agent. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Final act that satisfies the mission. |
| **G3.3: Handle Low Battery During Delivery** | If battery low during delivery, either return resource to checkpoint or hand over remaining task. | `FALLBACK(G3.3.1, G3.3.2)` | Perform | — | AND | Two alternatives are specified in the mission. |
| **G3.3.1: Return Resource to Checkpoint** | Return the resource to a checkpoint. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Required when battery < 30 % during delivery. |
| **G3.3.2: Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot** | Assign remaining delivery task to another robot. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Alternative to returning the resource. |
| **G3.3.1.1: Trigger Alert on Failure** | Trigger an alert if the robot fails to return the resource to a checkpoint. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Mission explicitly requires an alert on such failure. |
| **G3.3.1.2: Send Report to Sector Manager** | Send a report to the sector manager. | `-` | Perform | — | AND | Required after an alert has been triggered. |

