### 2. Task Table

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| **AT1: Estimate Waiting Time and Path** | Estimate waiting time and path to determine order of storage visits. | AND (to G2.1) | Robot’s current location | 1 | Only the robot that plans the route needs to perform this calculation. |
| **AT2: Move to Storage** | Navigate the robot to the specified storage location. | AND (to G2.2) | Storage location | 1 | A single robot must physically travel to the storage. |
| **AT3: Send Request Message** | Send a message to storage specifying the requested resources. | AND (to G2.3) | Robot at storage | 1 | Only the robot that is at the storage can send the request. |
| **AT4: Wait for Resource Retrieval** | Wait for the storage to retrieve the requested resources. | AND (to G2.4) | Storage location | 1 | The robot must wait for confirmation before proceeding. |
| **AT5: Pick Up Resources** | Pick up the retrieved resources from storage. | AND (to G2.5) | Storage location | 1 | Physical pickup is done by the robot that retrieved the resources. |
| **AT6: Move to Recharging Station** | Navigate to the recharging station to recharge battery. | AND (to G2.6.1) | Recharging station | 1 | Only the robot whose battery is low must go recharge. |
| **AT7: Assign Mission to Another Robot** | Assign the remaining collection task to another robot. | AND (to G2.6.2) | Current location | 1 | The robot handing over the task must inform the new robot. |
| **AT8: Move to Delivery Location** | Navigate to the delivery location where resources must be delivered. | AND (to G3.1) | Delivery location | 1 | The robot carrying the resources must travel to the delivery point. |
| **AT9: Deliver Resource** | Deliver the resources to the requesting agent at the delivery location. | AND (to G3.2) | Delivery location | 1 | Final act of the mission. |
| **AT10: Return Resource to Checkpoint** | Return the resource to a checkpoint due to low battery. | AND (to G3.3.1) | Checkpoint | 1 | Required when battery < 30 % during delivery. |
| **AT11: Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot** | Assign the remaining delivery task to another robot. | AND (to G3.3.2) | Current location | 1 | The robot handing over the delivery task must inform the new robot. |
| **AT12: Trigger Alert** | Trigger an alert if resource cannot be returned to checkpoint. | AND (to G3.3.1.1) | Robot’s current location | 1 | Mission explicitly requires an alert on such failure. |
| **AT13: Send Report** | Send a report to the sector manager after alert. | AND (to G3.3.1.2) | Robot’s current location | 1 | Required after an alert has been triggered. |

> **Parallelism**  
> The mission allows *multiple robots* to perform collection and delivery in parallel. In practice, the same set of tasks (AT1–AT5, AT8–AT9) can be instantiated for each robot that is assigned to a particular storage or delivery location. The runtime annotation `#` (parallel) is used at the high‑level goal level (e.g., G2 and G3 could be executed in parallel across different robots) but the sequential structure (`;`) is preserved for the **within‑robot** phases.

