### 4. Logical Relationships

| Parent → Children (Relation) | Runtime | Justification |
|------------------------------|---------|---------------|
| **G1 → G2, G3** | `;` (sequential) | Collection must finish before delivery can start. |
| **G2 → G2.1, G2.2, G2.3, G2.4, G2.5, G2.6** | `;` | All steps of collection are required. |
| **G3 → G3.1, G3.2, G3.3** | `;` | All steps of delivery are required. |
| **G2.6 → G2.6.1, G2.6.2** | `FALLBACK(G2.6.1, G2.6.2)` | Mission specifies two alternatives for low battery during collection. |
| **G3.3 → G3.3.1, G3.3.2** | `FALLBACK(G3.3.1, G3.3.2)` | Mission specifies two alternatives for low battery during delivery. |
| **G3.3.1 → G3.3.1.1, G3.3.1.2** | `;` | Alert and report must happen after resource is returned to checkpoint. |
| **G2.1 → AT1** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G2.2 → AT2** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G2.3 → AT3** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G2.4 → AT4** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G2.5 → AT5** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G2.6.1 → AT6** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G2.6.2 → AT7** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G3.1 → AT8** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G3.2 → AT9** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G3.3.1 → AT10** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G3.3.2 → AT11** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G3.3.1.1 → AT12** | `-` | Single task. |
| **G3.3.1.2 → AT13** | `-` | Single task. |

> **Parallel Execution**  
> While the top‑level mission is sequential, within each robot’s collection or delivery phase the robot can execute the sequence of tasks (`;`). If multiple robots are assigned, the *same* sub‑goal trees (G2, G3) can be instantiated in parallel, which is captured by the `#` operator at the high‑level (e.g., if the mission planner decides to run G2 and G3 in parallel across robots, the runtime annotation would be `#`). This is not shown explicitly in the table because the description only specifies parallelism **between** robots, not within a single robot’s execution path.

